Acceptance Criteria:
AC1: ApiRequest Model Enhancement
GIVEN existing ApiRequest model
WHEN enhancing for resource links support
THEN 
apiResourceLinks field is added as 

List<ApiResourceLink>
 

AND 
ApiResourceLink class includes 

categoryId, 

subcategoryId, 

title, 

url
 

AND all fields have appropriate validation annotations
AC2: Request Validation - Required Fields
GIVEN API creation request with resource links
WHEN validating request payload
THEN 
categoryId, 

subcategoryId, 

title, and 

url are required
 

AND validation errors return meaningful messages for missing fields
AC3: Request Validation - Category/Subcategory References
GIVEN API creation request with resource links
WHEN validating category and subcategory IDs
THEN 
categoryId must exist in 

api_resource_categories table
 

AND 
subcategoryId must exist in 

api_resource_subcategories table
 

AND 
subcategoryId must belong to the specified 

categoryId
 

AND validation errors return specific messages for invalid references
 

AC5: Database Transaction Processing
GIVEN valid API creation request with resource links
WHEN processing the request
THEN API creation and resource links insertion occur in single transaction
AND if API creation fails, no resource links are inserted
AND if resource links insertion fails, API creation is rolled back
AC6: Resource Links Storage
GIVEN successful API creation with resource links
WHEN storing resource links
THEN each link is inserted into 
api_resource_links table
 

AND 
api_family_id is populated from created API
 

AND 
created_ts and 

updated_ts are automatically set
 

AND all foreign key relationships are properly established
AC7: Empty Resource Links Handling
GIVEN API creation request without resource links
WHEN processing the request
THEN API is created successfully without resource links
AND no entries are made in 
api_resource_links table
 

AND existing API creation functionality remains unchanged
AC9: Service Layer Enhancement
GIVEN enhanced API creation functionality
WHEN implementing service layer changes
THEN 
ApiService.createNewApi() method handles resource links processing
 

AND separate method validates category/subcategory references
AND proper exception handling for validation and database errors
AND transactional annotations ensure data consistency
AC10: Repository Layer Enhancement
GIVEN resource links need database operations
WHEN implementing repository layer
THEN 
ApiResourceLinksRepository is created for CRUD operations
 

AND validation queries check category/subcategory existence and relationships
AND batch insert operations for multiple resource links
AND proper error handling for constraint violations
AC11: Error Response Standardization
GIVEN validation or processing errors occur
WHEN returning error responses
THEN errors follow standard format 
AND validation errors return HTTP 400 Bad Request
AND database errors return HTTP 500 Internal Server Error
AND error messages are specific and actionable
AC12: Backward Compatibility
GIVEN existing API creation requests without resource links
WHEN processing these requests
THEN requests continue to work without modification
AND response format remains consistent
AND no breaking changes to existing functionality
AC15: Performance Validation
GIVEN API creation with multiple resource links
WHEN processing requests with 10+ resource links
THEN response time remains within acceptable limits
AND database operations are optimized with batch processing
AND memory usage remains reasonable for large payloads
AC16: Logging Best Practices Implementation
GIVEN enhanced API creation functionality with resource links
WHEN implementing logging throughout the application
THEN INFO level logging includes only essential information (method entry, success/failure, key identifiers)
AND DEBUG level logging is used for detailed object contents and troubleshooting data
AND complete request/response objects are logged only at DEBUG level
AND INFO logs contain minimal context: 
"API creation started for apiName: {}, resourceLinks count: {}"
 

AND DEBUG logs contain full object details: 
"Full API request payload: {}"
 

AND ERROR logs include exception details without sensitive data
AND no sensitive information (tokens, passwords, personal data) is logged at any level
AND correlation IDs (trace-id, transaction-id) are included in all log levels for request tracking
